@lang pt
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp-dominio`
IMPORT `cp-pena`
IMPORT `cp-vigencias`

-- Código Penal (Decreto-Lei nº 2.848, de 1940): the whole encoding in one
-- module, and the encoding's main module.
--
-- Written at integration (integ-ctors, 2026-09-30). It holds no rules and no
-- directives. It imports every module that encodes the Code, in the Code's
-- order: the Parte Geral, then the Parte Especial's Títulos I to XII and the
-- Disposições Finais. Each group's `-comum` module comes first in its group.
-- g5 wrote both Título X and Título XII, so its two Título XII modules come
-- after g6b's Título XI.
--
-- Not imported: the tests modules (`*-testes.l4`), and the test fixtures
-- (`*-casos.l4`), which reuse fixture names on purpose (`Ana`, `um fato`) and
-- never meet, because each tests module imports its own.
--
-- The names that collided when every module first met here, and how each was
-- resolved, are in notes/integration.md ("integ-ctors").

-- g1a: Parte Geral, Títulos I a IV, arts. 1 a 31
IMPORT `cp-g1a-aplicacao`
IMPORT `cp-g1a-crime`
IMPORT `cp-g1a-erro`
IMPORT `cp-g1a-ilicitude`
IMPORT `cp-g1a-imputabilidade`
IMPORT `cp-g1a-concurso`

